# Machine-local paths. Copy this file to `paths.local.ps1` and edit it.
#
# `paths.local.ps1` is gitignored and is the ONLY place in this repository where a path
# on somebody's machine is allowed to live. Nothing else hardcodes one, so the repo is
# safe to publish and portable between machines without edits.
#
# Environment variables override these, so CI or a second machine can set
# MEVR_OPENXR_SDK / MEVR_GAME_BIN instead of writing this file at all.

# The OpenXR SDK, unpacked. Must contain include\ and native\Win32\release\{lib,bin}.
# Win32 (x86) is not optional - Mirror's Edge is a 32-bit process.
$OpenXrSdk = "X:\path\to\openxr-sdk"

# The Binaries folder of a DISPOSABLE copy of the game - the one `-Install` writes into.
# Do not point this at your only install; the mod drops a d3d9.dll next to the exe and
# testing means crashing the game repeatedly.
$GameBin = "X:\path\to\MirrorsEdge-Dev\Binaries"
